{
  "dom_id": "step-q275544",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be discrete random variables, and suppose $\\text{E}[X∣Y]=2Y-2.$ If $\\text{E}[X]=8,$ what is $\\text{E}[Y]?$",
  "worked_solution": "We are given an expression for $\\text{E}[X∣Y]$ in terms of $Y,$ and the value of $\\text{E}[X].$ This is a direct application of the tower property, which states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\text{E}[\\text{E}[X∣Y]].\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute the given expression for the inner expectation, which gives\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\text{E}[2Y-2].\n$$\n\nNow, we apply the linearity of expectation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =\\text{E}[2Y-2] \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that $\\text{E}[X]=8,$ so we solve this equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =2\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]-2 \\\\ 10 & =2\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
